[partC] non-interacting domain spacing d = 2*(r_loc + XC*sig_max) = 2*(1.5+2.0125) = 7.025; this demo's N=600 box (L=8.434) fits only the 2 domains built via the antipodal-offset trick (simple-cubic tiling gives floor(L/d)^3 = 1)
[partC] simple-cubic domain-packing projection: N=1e3 (L=10.00) -> floor(L/d)^3 = 1 simultaneous domains; N=1e4 (L=21.54) -> 27 simultaneous domains (ARITHMETIC EXTRAPOLATION -- only M=2 was built/tested here)
[partC] projected accepted-exchanges/wall-hour at 1 CPU-core-per-domain: N=600: 0/hr (1 domain); N=1e3: 0/hr (1 domain); N=1e4: 0/hr (27 domains, needs 27 cores to realize in wall-time, not just CPU-time)
[partC] TAKEAWAY: per-exchange CPU cost is flat in N (local moves only see ~|S| particles); PARALLEL WALL-CLOCK throughput scales ~ domains_fit(N) ~ O(N) once L exceeds ~2 domain-spacings (N gtrsim 2744), whereas a single glassy trajectory's tau_alpha cannot be parallelized at all -- this is the scalability lever the campaign deliverable needs.
